    ],
    "text": "Fungi that Change the Earth"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000011",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0010-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0000",
      "p0001-n0011-l0001",
      "p0001-n0011-l0002",
      "p0001-n0011-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The decomposition of organics by fungi plays a vital role in the natural carbon cycle. We are expected to determine the interactions among di\ufb00erent fungi and the impact of environmental \ufb02uctuations. In this paper, white-rot fungi, brown-rot fungi and Aspergillus niger are the main research objects for analysis. Three models are established."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0000",
      "p0001-n0012-l0001",
      "p0001-n0012-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Model I: Multi-Fungi Decomposition Model. First, based on the enzymatic reaction kinetic equation and Michaelis-Menten equation, we establish a single fungus decomposition model. Then, by introducing competitiveness index, the interactions of multiple fungi are described, and a multi-"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0003-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u53f7\uff1aMATHmodels"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0006"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0003",
      "p0001-n0012-l0004",
      "p0001-n0012-l0005",
      "p0001-n0012-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "fungi decomposition model is established. It is found that the combination of white-rot fungi and Aspergillus niger (WR & AN) would promote the decomposition of cellulose by Aspergillus niger; the combination of white-rot fungi and brown-rot fungi would inhibit the decomposition of lignin by white-rot fungi."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0006"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000",
      "p0001-n0013-l0001",
      "p0001-n0013-l0002",
      "p0001-n0013-l0003",
      "p0001-n0013-l0004",
      "p0001-n0013-l0005",
      "p0001-n0013-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Model II: Multi-Fungi Interactions Model. We establish Logistic growth retardation model and Lotka-Volterra population competition model to consider the impact of short-term and long- term interactions on fungal growth, respectively. In the short term (7 days), the growth of the three fungi is linear due to the su\ufb03cient resource; in the long term (500 days), the combination of white-rot fungi and Aspergillus niger, as well as the combination of brown-rot fungi and Aspergillus niger (BR & AN) can coexist, showing a promoting e\ufb00ect. However, the combination of white-rot fungi and brown-rot fungi has been eliminated from the population and cannot coexist."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0006"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0000",
      "p0001-n0014-l0001",
      "p0001-n0014-l0002",
      "p0001-n0014-l0003",
      "p0001-n0014-l0004",
      "p0001-n0014-l0005",
      "p0001-n0014-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Model III: Multi-Fungi-Interactions-Environment Model. First, we establish the relation- ship model of the growth rate with the environment, and determine the in\ufb02uence of two environ- mental variables on the fungal decomposition rate. Then, through sensitivity analysis of rapid environmental \ufb02uctuations, the decomposition rate trends under temperature and humidity changes are obtained. It is found that when the temperature changes, the fungi and their combinations that are suitable for the corresponding temperature have advantages; in the case of relatively low humidity, the fungi with high moisture tolerance and their combinations have advantages."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0005"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0015-l0000",
      "p0001-n0015-l0001",
      "p0001-n0015-l0002",
      "p0001-n0015-l0003",
      "p0001-n0015-l0004",
      "p0001-n0015-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "In addition, we predict the relative advantages and disadvantages in species and species combi- nations by calculating the decomposition rate under di\ufb00erent temperature and humidity conditions. We \ufb01nd that all species are at a disadvantage in the colder season of temperate zone and arid envi- ronment; in the warm season of temperate zone and semi-arid environment, BR and combinations of BR & AN have advantages, and WR and combinations of WR & AN have disadvantages; in tropical rain forests environments, the situation is reversed."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000019",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0016-l0000",
      "p0001-n0016-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Finally, we describe the impact of fungal species diversity on the ecosystem and summarize the importance of biodiversity: the increase in biodiversity can improve the environment\u2019s resilience."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000020",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "keywords",
